// services/chora-notifications/internal/adapter/http are the user-facing
// equivalents; gRPC is for internal service-to-service sync calls only
// (mTLS via Cloud Service Mesh per CLAUDE.md §4 protocol strategy).
//
// Primary callers (per docs/m13/grpc-mass-remediation-2026-05-16.md §4):
//   - chora-gateway BFF — proxies FE in-app notification routes
//   - chora-identity   — fires email-verified / closure-saga notifications
//   - chora-tenancy    — fires billing-related notifications
//   - chora-creation   — fires atom-published notifications to subscribers
//   - chora-sharing    — fires social-graph reaction / mention notifications
//   - chora-delivery   — fires assessment / certification notifications
//
// Aggregates exposed (per
// services/chora-notifications/internal/domain/notification/notification.go):
//   - Notification           — single delivery instance (email/push/in-app)
//   - NotificationTemplate   — append-only versioned content templates
//   - SubscriptionPreference — per-user opt-in/out, glob-matched by topic
//
// Append-only invariant (ddd-enforcement aggregate-invariant #4): template
// versions are immutable; mutation spawns a new version row.
//
// Cross-DB queries FORBIDDEN — atom_ids / gcid / tenant_id are cross-domain
// UUIDs referenced without FK constraint. Inter-domain side effects flow
// via Pub/Sub events (Protobuf Schema Registry validated).
//
// Deployed in chora-489812 team-platform pool. mTLS via Cloud Service Mesh;
// SPIFFE identity in mesh; W3C trace context in gRPC metadata.
